<x-public-layout title="Privacy Policy"><article class="container legal-content"><span class="eyebrow">YOUR INFORMATION, YOUR CONTROL</span><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p>ATS CV is in early access. This policy describes the account features currently available and the safeguards required before AI document features are enabled.</p><h2>Information we store</h2><p>When you register, we store your name, email address, a securely hashed password, and account verification information. Essential session cookies keep you signed in and protect forms against cross-site requests.</p><h2>CVs and external AI processing</h2><p>CV uploads and AI processing are not enabled in this release. When available, documents will be stored privately and shared with Google Gemini only after your explicit consent. Uploaded CVs and pasted descriptions will be treated as data, never as instructions. Avoid including sensitive details that are unnecessary for a job application.</p><h2>Access and deletion</h2><p>You can update your information, change your password, and delete your account in your profile. Account deletion removes the associated database records. Future document features must also remove privately stored files when documents or accounts are deleted.</p><h2>Operational records</h2><p>Application logs may include technical error information. In local development, email delivery uses the Laravel log mailer, so verification and reset links are recorded in the private application log. Production requires a configured email provider, protected logs, HTTPS, and an appropriate retention policy.</p><h2>Questions</h2><p>See the <a href="{{ route('contact') }}">Contact page</a> for support availability. This early-access policy must be reviewed with the deployment operator’s contact details and applicable privacy obligations before public launch.</p></article></x-public-layout>
